+The core results distinguish unavailable answers from selection failures. In the historical pool, 42 questions had no correct candidate; neither selector lost all correct candidates at eligibility. Scoring accounted for six failures and tie order for another 33 or 32 (Table~\ref{tab:failure-partition}). Validation-aware and complete-witness selection matched 99/180 and 100/180 references, versus 76/180 for C000 and 129/180 for the strongest fixed source (Table~\ref{tab:offline}). Both selectors had slot ties on 130 questions, but mixed-correctness top sets on 51. The diagnosis therefore distinguishes candidate availability, score discrimination, and unresolved ambiguity rather than treating every tie as a failure.
